before:
```typescript
function greeting(name: string, note?: string): string {
  return name + ": " + (note ?? "Welcome");
}
console.log(greeting("Ari"));
console.log(greeting("Ari", ""));
```

This prints Ari: Welcome and then Ari: followed by a space. greeting receives a required name and optional note, and returns a new string. ?? chooses Welcome only when note is missing or nullish; an explicitly supplied empty string remains empty. The optional type here does not allow null under strict checking.

after:
This function uses Welcome when note is missing.
```typescript
function greeting(name: string, note?: string): string {
  return name + ": " + (note ?? "Welcome");
}
console.log(greeting("Ari"));
```
The output is Ari: Welcome. If note is empty text, ?? keeps it empty.
